  "query_preview": "..\nKey Message 1: Shower chances now mainly confined to the western\nslopes.\n\nIncreased northwest flow will keep low clouds and scattered\nshowers around into Monday in the western slopes of WV into\nportion of SW VA/NW NC but should taper off going toward midday.\nHowever very well could see upslope clouds linger into Monday\nafternoon. A 40kt+ 8h jet will keep it gusty today especially \nthe mountains, with winds falling off by evening.\n\n\nKEY MESSAGE 2...Dry weather into midweek with temps above\nnormal. \n\nKeeping it dry into midweek and even late week looks like\nshowers may be just confined to the mountains. Ridge builds as\ndoes temps to above normal. Pattern change next weekend with\ndeeper trough and cool Canadian high moving in. Could be fairly\nbrisk Saturday.",
